gateway.bind from config file, not just env var (#55082)\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-03-27T01:21:17Z\"},{\"author\":{\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjI2MDY3MTI3\",\"is_bot\":false,\"login\":\"MoerAI\",\"name\":\"ToToKr\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACV-EDaQ\",\"name\":\"gateway\",\"description\":\"Gateway runtime\",\"color\":\"d4c5f9\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACWBvHUw\",\"name\":\"cli\",\"description\":\"CLI command changes\",\"color\":\"0052cc\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2CwGA\",\"name\":\"size: S\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"b76e79\"}],\"number\":55448,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"fix(gateway): resolve env-backed SecretRef in restart drift-check (#55029)\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-03-27T01:23:41Z\"},{\"author\":{\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjI2MDY3MTI3\",\"is_bot\":false,\"login\":\"MoerAI\",\"name\":\"ToToKr\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACV-ECIA\",\"name\":\"channel: whatsapp-web\",\"description\":\"Channel integration: whatsapp-web\",\"color\":\"1d76db\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"b76e79\"}],\"number\":55447,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"fix(whatsapp): add DM self-echo dedup for personal-number setups (#55426)\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-03-27T01:21:49Z\"},{\"author\":{\"id\":\"U_kgDODhk6WA\",\"is_bot\":false,\"login\":\"factnest365-ops\",\"name\":\"\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACWDenbg\",\"name\":\"agents\",\"description\":\"Agent runtime and tooling\",\"color\":\"5319e7\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"b76e79\"}],\"number\":55442,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"fix: allow memory_search and memory_get in sub-agent sessions (#55385)\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-03-27T01:19:13Z\"},{\"author\":{\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MzIwNzc3\",\"is_bot\":false,\"login\":\"lml2468\",\"name\":\"Menglin Li\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACV-EBOg\",\"name\":\"channel: msteams\",\"description\":\"Channel integration: msteams\",\"color\":\"1d76db\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2CwGA\",\"name\":\"size: S\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"b76e79\"}],\"number\":55440,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"fix(msteams): prevent path-to-regexp crash with express 5 (#55161)\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-03-27T01:14:45Z\"},{\"author\":{\"id\":\"U_kgDOBY2nAg\",\"is_bot\":false,\"login\":\"kinfey\",\"name\":\"Kinfey\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACWDenbg\",\"name\":\"agents\",\"description\":\"Agent runtime and tooling\",\"color\":\"5319e7\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOQb6kR88AAAACX2Cv9Q\",\"name\":\"size: XS\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"b76e79\"}],\"number\":55435,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"fix: WSL2 Ollama networking and provider discovery diagnostics\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-03-27T01:46:28Z\"}]","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774577185388}}
{"type":"message","id":"79fe90af","parentId":"3758444f","timestamp":"2026-03-27T02:06:50.559Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There are many new PRs and issues. Let me focus on the most interesting ones for potential review or investigation.\n\nLooking at recent PRs:\n\n1. **#55479** - External skills not injected into multi-agent specialist runtime (bug) - This is interesting\n2. **#55478** - Weixin message send misclassified as poll creation (bug) - We don't have weixin context\n3. **#55474** - Discord session.resetTriggers matches !new but sessionId doesn't rotate (bug) - could be interesting\n4. **#55472** - Gateway config reload corrupts agents.defaults.model (bug) - interesting\n5. **#55468** - Feature: Expose messageId in message_sent plugin hook - good feature request\n6. **#55462** - Telegram callback_query should include message_id - bug, small\n\nFor PRs:\n\n\nI'm noticing several smaller fixes from MoerAI across different modules like agents, slack, and gateway components, plus some documentation work and a particularly large PR about surfacing memory probe errors that stands out as potentially significant.\n\nLooking at what might be worth reviewing, #55458 with the memory probe errors issue seems substantial given its scope, and #55472 about the gateway config reload corruption could be impactful since it directly affects stability. I'm also tracking the #55437 subagent announce issue which was previously referenced but now appears closed.\n\nFor my reviews, I should focus on PRs that align with my expertise—Feishu, diagnostics, gateway, and agents—rather than spreading attention thin across everything. Let me prioritize the ones most relevant to my focus areas and where I can provide meaningful feedback. Looking at the regression issue, the `[Bug]: Non-compliant` title is too vague to assess without more context. The `EPERM` error on Windows with symlinks seems like a solid XS-sized bug with clear steps to reproduce. For #55451, exposing raw provider errors would be a useful diagnostic improvement, though it's labeled as a feature request rather than a bug fix.\n\nGiven my focus areas, I should prioritize reviewing #55479 on external skills injection since it's agent-related, #55466 on Feishu card content parsing as a channel issue, and #55437 on subagent announce failures as an agent runtime problem. These align better with my stated interests than the others. I'm seeing several PRs worth reviewing - the LiteLLM metadata stamping, the ACPX registry alignment (which is maintainer-authored), the Gateway startup degradation, and the Feishu CardKit streaming fix. But I should really focus on which ones align best with my interests in diagnostics, Feishu, and gateway functionality rather than spreading myself too thin across all the Slack, agents, and general infrastructure work.\n\nThe Feishu CardKit streaming card fix looks most relevant given my channel focus, so I'll dig into that one first to understand the actual problem being solved.","thinkingSignature":"6ae2eeae3b9e5cdd1d68b0ff548a2e6dcc58e3a3c93e566f7a2afb1899c1de5b"},{"type":"text","text":"今天 PR 非常活跃，筛选值得 focus 的目标：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_sa4yh49o9z6k_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh pr view 55466 --repo openclaw/openclaw --json body,files,additions,deletions,changedFiles,reviews 2>&1 | head -100","yieldMs":8000}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":11687,"output":679,"cacheRead":22191,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":34557,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774577185404}}
{"type":"message","id":"2a60abb9","parentId":"79fe90af","timestamp":"2026-03-27T02:06:51.087Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_sa4yh49o9z6k_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"additions\":185,\"body\":\"## Problem\\n\\nWhen reading messages that were sent as CardKit streaming cards (created via `POST /cardkit/v1/cards`), the IM API (`GET /im/v1/messages/{message_id}`) returns fallback content (a screenshot image + placeholder text like `[Interactive Card]`) instead of the actual card text content. This makes it impossible to retrieve the full text of bot replies that use streaming cards.\\n\\n## Root Cause\\n\\nCardKit streaming cards are referenced by `card_id` in the message body (`{\\\"type\\\":\\\"card\\\",\\\"data\\\":{\\\"card_id\\\":\\\"xxx\\\"}}`). The CardKit API only provides write endpoints — there is no read API to fetch card content by `card_id`. However, the IM message read API supports an undocumented query parameter `card_msg_content_type=raw_card_content` that instructs the API to inline the full card structure as a `json_card` field in the response content.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n### 1. Pass `card_msg_content_type` parameter\\n\\nAdd `card_msg_content_type: \\\"raw_card_content\\\"` to both:\\n- `client.im.message.get()` — used by `getMessageFeishu()` for single message reads\\n- `client.im.message.list()` — used by `listFeishuThreadMessages()` for thread history\\n\\n### 2. Parse `json_card` format in `parseInteractiveCardContent`\\n\\nBefore the existing element-based parsing, check for the `json_card` field (a JSON string) and extract text from:\\n- `config.summary.content` — the card summary (streaming cards write the full reply text here)\\n- `body.elements` — recursively extract `plain_text` and `markdown` nodes, including nested structures like `column_set`\\n\\nFalls through to the existing `elements` / `body.elements` parsing if `json_card` is absent or unparseable.\\n\\n### 3. Tests\\n\\nAdded 3 new test cases:\\n- Verifies `card_msg_content_type` param is passed to `message.get`\\n- Verifies `json_card` format is correctly parsed (summary + nested body elements)\\n- Verifies fallback to legacy elements when `json_card` contains invalid JSON\\n\\n## Related Issues\\n\\n- Relates to #54972 (CardKit streaming card content not readable)\\n- Relates to #48281 (Interactive card message parsing)\\n- Relates to #32930 (Message content retrieval improvements)\\n\\n## References\\n\\n- The official Lark plugin ([larksuite/openclaw-lark](https://github.com/nicepkg/openclaw-lark)) uses the same `card_msg_content_type=raw_card_content` parameter in its `fetchCardContent` function (`src/messaging/inbound/parse-io.ts`).\",\"changedFiles\":2,\"deletions\":8,\"files\":[{\"path\":\"extensions/feishu/src/send.test.ts\",\"additions\":105,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"extensions/feishu/src/send.ts\",\"additions\":80,\"deletions\":8,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"}],\"reviews\":[{\"id\":\"PRR_kwDOQb6kR87vhAJf\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"greptile-apps\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"body\":\"\",\"submittedAt\":\"2026-03-27T01:53:21Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"reactionGroups\":[],\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"commit\":{\"oid\":\"9649267f22b9ae8ded832adedb78581e23303ec6\"}},{\"id\":\"PRR_kwDOQb6kR87vhB3b\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"NONE\",\"body\":\"\\n### 💡 Codex Review\\n\\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\\n\\n**Reviewed commit:** `9649267f22`\\n    \\n\\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\\n<br/>\\n\\nCodex has been enabled to automatically review pull requests in this repo. Reviews are triggered when you\\n- Open a pull request for review\\n- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex review\\\".\\n\\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nWhen you [sign up for Codex through ChatGPT](https://openai.com/codex), Codex can also answer questions or update the PR, like \\\"@codex address that feedback\\\".\\n            \\n</details>\",\"submittedAt\":\"2026-03-27T01:55:39Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"reactionGroups\":[],\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"commit\":{\"oid\":\"9649267f22b9ae8ded832adedb78581e23303ec6\"}},{\"id\":\"PRR_kwDOQb6kR87vhIMi\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"NONE\",\"body\":\"\\n### 💡 Codex Review\\n\\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\\n\\n**Reviewed commit:** `cf582f3a5e`\\n    \\n\\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\\n<br/>\\n\\nCodex has been enabled to automatically review pull requests in this repo. Reviews are triggered when you\\n- Open a pull request for review\\n- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex review\\\".\\n\\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nWhen you [sign up for Codex through ChatGPT](https://openai.com/codex), Codex can also answer questions or update the PR, like \\\"@codex address that feedback\\\".\\n            \\n</details>\",\"submittedAt\":\"2026-03-27T02:06:19Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"reactionGroups\":[],\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"commit\":{\"oid\":\"cf582f3a5edd32500e77d49aa8cb58e4d96abbc6\"}}]}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":511,"aggregated":"{\"additions\":185,\"body\":\"## Problem\\n\\nWhen reading messages that were sent as CardKit streaming cards (created via `POST /cardkit/v1/cards`), the IM API (`GET /im/v1/messages/{message_id}`) returns fallback content (a screenshot image + placeholder text like `[Interactive Card]`) instead of the actual card text content. This makes it impossible to retrieve the full text of bot replies that use streaming cards.\\n\\n## Root Cause\\n\\nCardKit streaming cards are referenced by `card_id` in the message body (`{\\\"type\\\":\\\"card\\\",\\\"data\\\":{\\\"card_id\\\":\\\"xxx\\\"}}`). The CardKit API only provides write endpoints — there is no read API to fetch card content by `card_id`. However, the IM message read API supports an undocumented query parameter `card_msg_content_type=raw_card_content` that instructs the API to inline the full card structure as a `json_card` field in the response content.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n### 1. Pass `card_msg_content_type` parameter\\n\\nAdd `card_msg_content_type: \\\"raw_card_content\\\"` to both:\\n- `client.im.message.get()` — used by `getMessageFeishu()` for single message reads\\n- `client.im.message.list()` — used by `listFeishuThreadMessages()` for thread history\\n\\n### 2. Parse `json_card` format in `parseInteractiveCardContent`\\n\\nBefore the existing element-based parsing, check for the `json_card` field (a JSON string) and extract text from:\\n- `config.summary.content` — the card summary (streaming cards write the full reply text here)\\n- `body.elements` — recursively extract `plain_text` and `markdown` nodes, including nested structures like `column_set`\\n\\nFalls through to the existing `elements` / `body.elements` parsing if `json_card` is absent or unparseable.\\n\\n### 3. Tests\\n\\nAdded 3 new test cases:\\n- Verifies `card_msg_content_type` param is passed to `message.get`\\n- Verifies `json_card` format is correctly parsed (summary + nested body elements)\\n- Verifies fallback to legacy elements when `json_card` contains invalid JSON\\n\\n## Related Issues\\n\\n- Relates to #54972 (CardKit streaming card content not readable)\\n- Relates to #48281 (Interactive card message parsing)\\n- Relates to #32930 (Message content retrieval improvements)\\n\\n## References\\n\\n- The official Lark plugin ([larksuite/openclaw-lark](https://github.com/nicepkg/openclaw-lark)) uses the same `card_msg_content_type=raw_card_content` parameter in its `fetchCardContent` function (`src/messaging/inbound/parse-io.ts`).\",\"changedFiles\":2,\"deletions\":8,\"files\":[{\"path\":\"extensions/feishu/src/send.test.ts\",\"additions\":105,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"extensions/feishu/src/send.ts\",\"additions\":80,\"deletions\":8,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"}],\"reviews\":[{\"id\":\"PRR_kwDOQb6kR87vhAJf\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"greptile-apps\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"body\":\"\",\"submittedAt\":\"2026-03-27T01:53:21Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"reactionGroups\":[],\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"commit\":{\"oid\":\"9649267f22b9ae8ded832adedb78581e23303ec6\"}},{\"id\":\"PRR_kwDOQb6kR87vhB3b\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"NONE\",\"body\":\"\\n### 💡 Codex Review\\n\\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\\n\\n**Reviewed commit:** `9649267f22`\\n    \\n\\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\\n<br/>\\n\\nCodex has been enabled to automatically review pull requests in this repo. Reviews are triggered when you\\n- Open a pull request for review\\n- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex review\\\".\\n\\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nWhen you [sign up for Codex through ChatGPT](https://openai.com/codex), Codex can also answer questions or update the PR, like \\\"@codex address that feedback\\\".\\n            \\n</details>\",\"submittedAt\":\"2026-03-27T01:55:39Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"reactionGroups\":[],\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"commit\":{\"oid\":\"9649267f22b9ae8ded832adedb78581e23303ec6\"}},{\"id\":\"PRR_kwDOQb6kR87vhIMi\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"NONE\",\"body\":\"\\n### 💡 Codex Review\\n\\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\\n\\n**Reviewed commit:** `cf582f3a5e`\\n    \\n\\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\\n<br/>\\n\\nCodex has been enabled to automatically review pull requests in this repo. Reviews are triggered when you\\n- Open a pull request for review\\n- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex review\\\".\\n\\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nWhen you [sign up for Codex through ChatGPT](https://openai.com/codex), Codex can also answer questions or update the PR, like \\\"@codex address that feedback\\\".\\n            \\n</details>\",\"submittedAt\":\"2026-03-27T02:06:19Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"reactionGroups\":[],\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"commit\":{\"oid\":\"cf582f3a5edd32500e77d49aa8cb58e4d96abbc6\"}}]}","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774577211070}}
{"type":"message","id":"e25c79f1","parentId":"2a60abb9","timestamp":"2026-03-27T02:07:02.734Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. This is a well-structured PR with a clear fix for a Feishu-specific issue. The fix addresses:\n1. Adding `card_msg_content_type: \"raw_card_content\"` to Feishu IM API calls\n2. Parsing the `json_card` format in `parseInteractiveCardContent`\n\nIt's XS (185 additions, 8 deletions), and the Greptile review already commented. Let me check what Greptile said.","thinkingSignature":"db3e340dc570b49e87e51da4f7b7d41780410f55a1b3c6d212c1516fc2f877ae"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_2yz5112iz0zk_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh pr view 55466 --repo openclaw/openclaw --json body 2>&1 | jq -r '.body' | head -20; echo \"---\"; gh api repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/55466/comments 2>&1 | jq '.[].body' | head -50","yieldMs":8000}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":13692,"output":191,"cacheRead":22191,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":36074,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774577211086}}
{"type":"message","id":"7a875433","parentId":"e25c79f1","timestamp":"2026-03-27T02:07:03.661Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_2yz5112iz0zk_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Problem\n\nWhen reading messages that were sent as CardKit streaming cards (created via `POST /cardkit/v1/cards`), the IM API (`GET /im/v1/messages/{message_id}`) returns fallback content (a screenshot image + placeholder text like `[Interactive Card]`) instead of the actual card text content. This makes it impossible to retrieve the full text of bot replies that use streaming cards.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nCardKit streaming cards are referenced by `card_id` in the message body (`{\"type\":\"card\",\"data\":{\"card_id\":\"xxx\"}}`). The CardKit API only provides write endpoints — there is no read API to fetch card content by `card_id`. However, the IM message read API supports an undocumented query parameter `card_msg_content_type=raw_card_content` that instructs the API to inline the full card structure as a `json_card` field in the response content.\n\n## Fix\n\n### 1. Pass `card_msg_content_type` parameter\n\nAdd `card_msg_content_type: \"raw_card_content\"` to both:\n- `client.im.message.get()` — used by `getMessageFeishu()` for single message reads\n- `client.im.message.list()` — used by `listFeishuThreadMessages()` for thread history\n\n### 2. Parse `json_card` format in `parseInteractiveCardContent`\n\nBefore the existing element-based parsing, check for the `json_card` field (a JSON string) and extract text from:\n- `config.summary.content` — the card summary (streaming cards write the full reply text here)\n---\n\"<a href=\\\"#\\\"><img alt=\\\"P2\\\" src=\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=7\\\" align=\\\"top\\\"></a> **`rows` field typed but never recursed into**\\n\\nThe node type includes `rows?: unknown[]`, and the comment references \\\"form elements, etc.\\\" as a motivation for recursion — but there is no corresponding loop over `rows`. Any CardKit elements that store text inside rows (e.g., a `form` element with row-based layout) would be silently skipped.\\n\\nEither add the recursion or remove the `rows` field from the type to keep the declared surface and the implementation in sync:\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    const node = el as {\\n      tag?: string;\\n      property?: { content?: string };\\n      elements?: unknown[];\\n      columns?: unknown[];\\n    };\\n    if (node.tag === \\\"plain_text\\\" && typeof node.property?.content === \\\"string\\\") {\\n      texts.push(node.property.content);\\n    }\\n    if (node.tag === \\\"markdown\\\" && typeof (node as { content?: string }).content === \\\"string\\\") {\\n      texts.push((node as { content?: string }).content!);\\n    }\\n    // Recurse into nested structures (column_set columns, form elements, etc.)\\n    if (Array.isArray(node.elements)) {\\n      texts.push(...extractJsonCardTexts(node.elements));\\n    }\\n    if (Array.isArray(node.columns)) {\\n      for (const col of node.columns) {\\n        if (\\n          col &&\\n          typeof col === \\\"object\\\" &&\\n          Array.isArray((col as { elements?: unknown[] }).elements)\\n        ) {\\n          texts.push(...extractJsonCardTexts((col as { elements: unknown[] }).elements));\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n```\\n\\nOr, if rows are intentionally planned for the future, add a `// TODO: recurse into rows` comment so it is not forgotten.\\n\\n<details><summary>Prompt To Fix With AI</summary>\\n\\n`````markdown\\nThis is a comment left during a code review.\\nPath: extensions/feishu/src/send.ts\\nLine: 189-212\\n\\nComment:\\n**`rows` field typed but never recursed into**\\n\\nThe node type includes `rows?: unknown[]`, and the comment references \\\"form elements, etc.\\\" as a motivation for recursion — but there is no corresponding loop over `rows`. Any CardKit elements that store text inside rows (e.g., a `form` element with row-based layout) would be silently skipped.\\n\\nEither add the recursion or remove the `rows` field from the type to keep the declared surface and the implementation in sync:\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    const node = el as {\\n      tag?: string;\\n      property?: { content?: string };\\n      elements?: unknown[];\\n      columns?: unknown[];\\n    };\\n    if (node.tag === \\\"plain_text\\\" && typeof node.property?.content === \\\"string\\\") {\\n      texts.push(node.property.content);\\n    }\\n    if (node.tag === \\\"markdown\\\" && typeof (node as { content?: string }).content === \\\"string\\\") {\\n      texts.push((node as { content?: string }).content!);\\n    }\\n    // Recurse into nested structures (column_set columns, form elements, etc.)\\n    if (Array.isArray(node.elements)) {\\n      texts.push(...extractJsonCardTexts(node.elements));\\n    }\\n    if (Array.isArray(node.columns)) {\\n      for (const col of node.columns) {\\n        if (\\n          col &&\\n          typeof col === \\\"object\\\" &&\\n          Array.isArray((col as { elements?: unknown[] }).elements)\\n        ) {\\n          texts.push(...extractJsonCardTexts((col as { elements: unknown[] }).elements));\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n```\\n\\nOr, if rows are intentionally planned for the future, add a `// TODO: recurse into rows` comment so it is not forgotten.\\n\\nHow can I resolve this? If you propose a fix, please make it concise.\\n`````\\n</details>\"\n\"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Restore type safety for Feishu list query params**\\n\\nThis change introduces `// eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any` and `const listParams: any`, which violates the documented repo rule in `AGENTS.md` (“Never add `@ts-nocheck` and do not disable `no-explicit-any`”). More importantly, it removes compile-time validation for the `message.list` query shape, so future SDK type changes or param typos here can silently pass CI and only fail when thread reads run in production; please use a typed local param shape (or a narrowly scoped cast) instead of disabling the rule.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n\"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Parse top-level json_card elements**\\n\\nWith `card_msg_content_type=raw_card_content`, interactive messages can be wrapped as `{\\\"json_card\\\":\\\"...\\\"}`. This new branch only reads `jsonCard.body.elements`, but schema 1.0 cards store textual blocks in top-level `elements` (which the legacy parser path already handled). In that case `parts` stays empty, then fallback parsing runs against the wrapper object (not the parsed card), and the function returns `[Interactive Card]` instead of the actual text. Please also extract from `jsonCard.elements` before falling through.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\""}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":903,"aggregated":"## Problem\n\nWhen reading messages that were sent as CardKit streaming cards (created via `POST /cardkit/v1/cards`), the IM API (`GET /im/v1/messages/{message_id}`) returns fallback content (a screenshot image + placeholder text like `[Interactive Card]`) instead of the actual card text content. This makes it impossible to retrieve the full text of bot replies that use streaming cards.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nCardKit streaming cards are referenced by `card_id` in the message body (`{\"type\":\"card\",\"data\":{\"card_id\":\"xxx\"}}`). The CardKit API only provides write endpoints — there is no read API to fetch card content by `card_id`. However, the IM message read API supports an undocumented query parameter `card_msg_content_type=raw_card_content` that instructs the API to inline the full card structure as a `json_card` field in the response content.\n\n## Fix\n\n### 1. Pass `card_msg_content_type` parameter\n\nAdd `card_msg_content_type: \"raw_card_content\"` to both:\n- `client.im.message.get()` — used by `getMessageFeishu()` for single message reads\n- `client.im.message.list()` — used by `listFeishuThreadMessages()` for thread history\n\n### 2. Parse `json_card` format in `parseInteractiveCardContent`\n\nBefore the existing element-based parsing, check for the `json_card` field (a JSON string) and extract text from:\n- `config.summary.content` — the card summary (streaming cards write the full reply text here)\n---\n\"<a href=\\\"#\\\"><img alt=\\\"P2\\\" src=\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=7\\\" align=\\\"top\\\"></a> **`rows` field typed but never recursed into**\\n\\nThe node type includes `rows?: unknown[]`, and the comment references \\\"form elements, etc.\\\" as a motivation for recursion — but there is no corresponding loop over `rows`. Any CardKit elements that store text inside rows (e.g., a `form` element with row-based layout) would be silently skipped.\\n\\nEither add the recursion or remove the `rows` field from the type to keep the declared surface and the implementation in sync:\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    const node = el as {\\n      tag?: string;\\n      property?: { content?: string };\\n      elements?: unknown[];\\n      columns?: unknown[];\\n    };\\n    if (node.tag === \\\"plain_text\\\" && typeof node.property?.content === \\\"string\\\") {\\n      texts.push(node.property.content);\\n    }\\n    if (node.tag === \\\"markdown\\\" && typeof (node as { content?: string }).content === \\\"string\\\") {\\n      texts.push((node as { content?: string }).content!);\\n    }\\n    // Recurse into nested structures (column_set columns, form elements, etc.)\\n    if (Array.isArray(node.elements)) {\\n      texts.push(...extractJsonCardTexts(node.elements));\\n    }\\n    if (Array.isArray(node.columns)) {\\n      for (const col of node.columns) {\\n        if (\\n          col &&\\n          typeof col === \\\"object\\\" &&\\n          Array.isArray((col as { elements?: unknown[] }).elements)\\n        ) {\\n          texts.push(...extractJsonCardTexts((col as { elements: unknown[] }).elements));\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n```\\n\\nOr, if rows are intentionally planned for the future, add a `// TODO: recurse into rows` comment so it is not forgotten.\\n\\n<details><summary>Prompt To Fix With AI</summary>\\n\\n`````markdown\\nThis is a comment left during a code review.\\nPath: extensions/feishu/src/send.ts\\nLine: 189-212\\n\\nComment:\\n**`rows` field typed but never recursed into**\\n\\nThe node type includes `rows?: unknown[]`, and the comment references \\\"form elements, etc.\\\" as a motivation for recursion — but there is no corresponding loop over `rows`. Any CardKit elements that store text inside rows (e.g., a `form` element with row-based layout) would be silently skipped.\\n\\nEither add the recursion or remove the `rows` field from the type to keep the declared surface and the implementation in sync:\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    const node = el as {\\n      tag?: string;\\n      property?: { content?: string };\\n      elements?: unknown[];\\n      columns?: unknown[];\\n    };\\n    if (node.tag === \\\"plain_text\\\" && typeof node.property?.content === \\\"string\\\") {\\n      texts.push(node.property.content);\\n    }\\n    if (node.tag === \\\"markdown\\\" && typeof (node as { content?: string }).content === \\\"string\\\") {\\n      texts.push((node as { content?: string }).content!);\\n    }\\n    // Recurse into nested structures (column_set columns, form elements, etc.)\\n    if (Array.isArray(node.elements)) {\\n      texts.push(...extractJsonCardTexts(node.elements));\\n    }\\n    if (Array.isArray(node.columns)) {\\n      for (const col of node.columns) {\\n        if (\\n          col &&\\n          typeof col === \\\"object\\\" &&\\n          Array.isArray((col as { elements?: unknown[] }).elements)\\n        ) {\\n          texts.push(...extractJsonCardTexts((col as { elements: unknown[] }).elements));\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n```\\n\\nOr, if rows are intentionally planned for the future, add a `// TODO: recurse into rows` comment so it is not forgotten.\\n\\nHow can I resolve this? If you propose a fix, please make it concise.\\n`````\\n</details>\"\n\"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Restore type safety for Feishu list query params**\\n\\nThis change introduces `// eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any` and `const listParams: any`, which violates the documented repo rule in `AGENTS.md` (“Never add `@ts-nocheck` and do not disable `no-explicit-any`”). More importantly, it removes compile-time validation for the `message.list` query shape, so future SDK type changes or param typos here can silently pass CI and only fail when thread reads run in production; please use a typed local param shape (or a narrowly scoped cast) instead of disabling the rule.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n\"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Parse top-level json_card elements**\\n\\nWith `card_msg_content_type=raw_card_content`, interactive messages can be wrapped as `{\\\"json_card\\\":\\\"...\\\"}`. This new branch only reads `jsonCard.body.elements`, but schema 1.0 cards store textual blocks in top-level `elements` (which the legacy parser path already handled). In that case `parts` stays empty, then fallback parsing runs against the wrapper object (not the parsed card), and the function returns `[Interactive Card]` instead of the actual text. Please also extract from `jsonCard.elements` before falling through.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774577223637}}
{"type":"message","id":"8fed9fb6","parentId":"7a875433","timestamp":"2026-03-27T02:07:22.671Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! The Greptile reviews on #55466 are very detailed and point out real issues:\n\n1. **P1**: `rows` field typed but never recursed into - suggests adding rows recursion\n2. **P1**: Restore type safety - using `any` and disabling TS rules\n3. **P1**: Parse top-level `json_card.elements` - missing handling of top-level elements\n\nThis is a high-quality PR with real feedback. Let me also check the other PRs more quickly.\n\nLet me now think about what to do:\n1. **#55466** (feishu CardKit): Greptile has substantive P1 comments - worth doing a thorough review myself and potentially providing an Approve with notes\n\n\n2. **#55473** (gateway startup secret failures) - looks minor from the description\n3. **#55479** (external skills not injected): This is a significant bug I should investigate further\n\nI'm noticing these recent PRs from MoerAI like #55471 (slack), #55469 (agents), and #55467 (agents) are all XS fixes, but I'm already behind on reviews for #55153 and #55137. I need to prioritize which ones are worth my focused attention versus which ones I can skim through. I should wrap up my review of #55466 since Greptile has already provided solid feedback there, and focus my attention on the external skills injection bug (#55479) which seems more critical.","thinkingSignature":"62d6bc4bd0cdbbe6dee011557490c50cb46dcee05f60f605815c91808085a43c"},{"type":"text","text":"#55466 有 Greptile 详细 P1 review，质量不错。深入看一下 #55479（external skills 未注入）：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_g85qhzwdkmkj_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh pr view 55479 --repo openclaw/openclaw --json body,files,additions,deletions,changedFiles,reviews 2>&1 | jq '{body: .body, files: .files, additions: .additions, deletions: .deletions, changedFiles: .changedFiles, reviews: [.reviews[] | {author: .author.login, state: .state, body: (.body | if length > 200 then .[0:200] + \"...\" else . end)}]}'","yieldMs":8000}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":15485,"output":476,"cacheRead":22191,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":38152,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774577223660}}
