{"type":"message","id":"925ec3d4","parentId":"fecb670e","timestamp":"2026-03-27T02:07:35.306Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Hmm, it's an issue, not a PR. Let me check the issue instead.","thinkingSignature":"fe5948573c05c630c25b9c81eb3da8cd7fd48ca1dd2378be2482b615b22e4974"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_f3fa5iurr4ft_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh issue view 55479 --repo openclaw/openclaw 2>&1 | head -80","yieldMs":8000}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":16422,"output":74,"cacheRead":22191,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":38687,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774577252761}}
{"type":"message","id":"c0ebe7e3","parentId":"925ec3d4","timestamp":"2026-03-27T02:07:36.118Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_f3fa5iurr4ft_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"title:\t[Bug] External skills are ready but not injected into multi-agent specialist runtime in v2026.3.24\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tIanYang868\nlabels:\tbug, bug:behavior\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nnumber:\t55479\n--\n### Bug type\n\nBehavior bug (incorrect output/state without crash)\n\n### Beta release blocker\n\nNo\n\n### Summary\n\nIn v2026.3.24, external skills marked ready are not injected into specialist agents’ runtime prompt in multi-agent setups.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Install OpenClaw v2026.3.24 and create a multi-agent setup with `main` plus at least one specialist agent (for example `investor`).\n2. Install external skills such as `engram`, `summarize`, `web-content-fetcher`, and `web-search` under `~/.openclaw/skills`.\n3. Also install the same skills under the specialist agent workspace, e.g. `~/.openclaw/workspace-investor/skills`.\n4. Run `openclaw skills list` and confirm those external skills are shown as ready.\n5. Run a fresh-session local test such as:\n   `openclaw agent --agent investor --local --session-id repro-skill-investor-1 --message \"Only list the currently visible skill names.\" --json`\n6. Inspect `systemPromptReport.skills.entries` in the JSON output.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe external skills should appear in `systemPromptReport.skills.entries` for the specialist agent when they are installed under either `~/.openclaw/skills` or the agent’s own `<workspace>/skills`.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n`openclaw skills list` shows the external skills as ready, but the specialist agent runtime only receives bundled skills in `systemPromptReport.skills.entries`. The external skills (`engram`, `summarize`, `web-content-fetcher`, `web-search`) do not appear.\n\n### OpenClaw version\n\n2026.3.24\n\n### Operating system\n\nmacOS 15.4\n\n### Install method\n\nnpm global\n\n### Model\n\nopenai/gpt-5.4\n\n### Provider / routing chain\n\nopenclaw -> PackyAPI -> openai/gpt-5.4\n\n### Additional provider/model setup details\n\nModel/auth was working normally through PackyAPI. `main` and specialist agents could successfully call `openai/gpt-5.4`, so this does not appear to be an auth, provider, or network failure. The problem only affected external skill injection into specialist runtime.\n\n### Logs, screenshots, and evidence\n\n```shell\nEvidence 1: `openclaw skills list`\nThe external skills were recognized as ready by `openclaw skills list`, including:\n- summarize\n- web-content-fetcher\n- web-search\n\nEvidence 2: specialist runtime JSON\nIn specialist agent JSON output, `systemPromptReport.skills.entries` only contained bundled skills:\n- clawhub\n- coding-agent\n- gh-issues\n- github\n- healthcheck"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":793,"aggregated":"title:\t[Bug] External skills are ready but not injected into multi-agent specialist runtime in v2026.3.24\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tIanYang868\nlabels:\tbug, bug:behavior\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nnumber:\t55479\n--\n### Bug type\n\nBehavior bug (incorrect output/state without crash)\n\n### Beta release blocker\n\nNo\n\n### Summary\n\nIn v2026.3.24, external skills marked ready are not injected into specialist agents’ runtime prompt in multi-agent setups.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Install OpenClaw v2026.3.24 and create a multi-agent setup with `main` plus at least one specialist agent (for example `investor`).\n2. Install external skills such as `engram`, `summarize`, `web-content-fetcher`, and `web-search` under `~/.openclaw/skills`.\n3. Also install the same skills under the specialist agent workspace, e.g. `~/.openclaw/workspace-investor/skills`.\n4. Run `openclaw skills list` and confirm those external skills are shown as ready.\n5. Run a fresh-session local test such as:\n   `openclaw agent --agent investor --local --session-id repro-skill-investor-1 --message \"Only list the currently visible skill names.\" --json`\n6. Inspect `systemPromptReport.skills.entries` in the JSON output.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe external skills should appear in `systemPromptReport.skills.entries` for the specialist agent when they are installed under either `~/.openclaw/skills` or the agent’s own `<workspace>/skills`.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n`openclaw skills list` shows the external skills as ready, but the specialist agent runtime only receives bundled skills in `systemPromptReport.skills.entries`. The external skills (`engram`, `summarize`, `web-content-fetcher`, `web-search`) do not appear.\n\n### OpenClaw version\n\n2026.3.24\n\n### Operating system\n\nmacOS 15.4\n\n### Install method\n\nnpm global\n\n### Model\n\nopenai/gpt-5.4\n\n### Provider / routing chain\n\nopenclaw -> PackyAPI -> openai/gpt-5.4\n\n### Additional provider/model setup details\n\nModel/auth was working normally through PackyAPI. `main` and specialist agents could successfully call `openai/gpt-5.4`, so this does not appear to be an auth, provider, or network failure. The problem only affected external skill injection into specialist runtime.\n\n### Logs, screenshots, and evidence\n\n```shell\nEvidence 1: `openclaw skills list`\nThe external skills were recognized as ready by `openclaw skills list`, including:\n- summarize\n- web-content-fetcher\n- web-search\n\nEvidence 2: specialist runtime JSON\nIn specialist agent JSON output, `systemPromptReport.skills.entries` only contained bundled skills:\n- clawhub\n- coding-agent\n- gh-issues\n- github\n- healthcheck","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774577256099}}
{"type":"message","id":"1e4e9341","parentId":"c0ebe7e3","timestamp":"2026-03-27T02:08:01.232Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a good bug report - it has clear reproduction steps, expected vs actual behavior, and version info. However, this is a regression bug that likely requires:\n1. Understanding the code that handles external skill injection\n2. Finding what changed in v2026.3.24 that caused the regression\n\nThis is more complex than a docs fix. Let me think about whether this is something we should work on:- It's a regression bug in multi-agent specialist runtime- It requires understanding the skill injection code\n- It may require significant investigation\n\nGiven our resources, this might be better as a well-documented issue (similar to our P1 approach) rather than a PR we write ourselves. \n\nI should note that MoerAI already submitted PR #55469 to address the subagent announce issue, so I should check if that's related to this external skills problem. I'm also seeing several other PRs worth reviewing - the LiteLLM metadata one, the ACPX registry alignment, and the gateway secret failures fix - but I need to prioritize whether to investigate this bug further or focus on reviewing existing PRs.\n\nGiven my constraint of one review per day and limited bandwidth, I should probably spend my time on #55466 since it has Greptile reviews I can build on, rather than spreading myself thin across all these PRs. The regression bug #55479 is worth documenting as an issue with a solid description, but I should be strategic about whether I open that myself or let the community handle it. The LiteLLM metadata stamping in #55477 is a feature request, not a bug fix, so it doesn't align with the project's focus on confirmed bugs and documentation gaps.\n\nMy next steps are to do a thorough review of #55466 since it has substantive feedback already, and either open an issue for #55479 or hand it off to xixi for more investigation before committing to it.","thinkingSignature":"3eaef12bde91396bb956783bbe116459d07e29e783a21b4ac0700de032b2eda9"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] **Provider 配置提案已记录搁置，OpenClaw 项目继续。**\n\n---\n\n**📊 快速扫描结果（2026-03-27 10:10）**\n\n最近 24h 新增 **20+ issues / 25+ PRs**，筛选出最值得关注的：\n\n| # | 类型 | 标题 | 价值 | 行动 |\n|---|------|------|------|------|\n| #55466 | **PR（feishu）** | CardKit streaming card 文本读取修复 | ⭐⭐⭐ | 立即 review |\n| #55479 | **Issue（bug）** | External skills 未注入 specialist runtime | ⭐⭐⭐ | 确认是否 regression |\n| #55477 | PR | LiteLLM request metadata 打标 | ⭐⭐ | 可 review |\n| #55473 | PR | Gateway startup secret failures 处理 | ⭐⭐ | 可 review |\n\n**#55466 是 Feishu channel PR**，已有 Greptile 发出 3 条 P1 反馈（含 2 个实质性代码问题），这是我们的强项赛道，立即 review。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_iiaju6b1ld3l_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh api repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/55466/files --jq '.[].filename' 2>&1","yieldMs":8000}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":17145,"output":675,"cacheRead":22191,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":40011,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774577256117}}
{"type":"message","id":"5dc14fa0","parentId":"1e4e9341","timestamp":"2026-03-27T02:08:01.795Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_iiaju6b1ld3l_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"extensions/feishu/src/send.test.ts\nextensions/feishu/src/send.ts"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":545,"aggregated":"extensions/feishu/src/send.test.ts\nextensions/feishu/src/send.ts","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774577281779}}
{"type":"message","id":"314387d0","parentId":"5dc14fa0","timestamp":"2026-03-27T02:08:05.947Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The PR only modifies 2 files in the feishu extension. Let me look at the actual code changes.","thinkingSignature":"57d8efbede29738f259050cbe6d8ebc291f4645065aba92bc1e38169dedf1118"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_8gv1h3wdmptr_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh api repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/55466/files --jq '.[0:2] | .[] | {filename, status, additions, deletions, patch}' 2>&1 | head -200","yieldMs":8000}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":17856,"output":104,"cacheRead":22191,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":40151,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774577281794}}
{"type":"message","id":"6ea5e5e5","parentId":"314387d0","timestamp":"2026-03-27T02:08:06.392Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_8gv1h3wdmptr_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"additions\":105,\"deletions\":0,\"filename\":\"extensions/feishu/src/send.test.ts\",\"patch\":\"@@ -60,6 +60,111 @@ describe(\\\"getMessageFeishu\\\", () =\\u003e {\\n     });\\n   });\\n \\n+  it(\\\"passes card_msg_content_type param to message.get\\\", async () =\\u003e {\\n+    mockClientGet.mockResolvedValueOnce({\\n+      code: 0,\\n+      data: {\\n+        items: [\\n+          {\\n+            message_id: \\\"om_param\\\",\\n+            chat_id: \\\"oc_param\\\",\\n+            msg_type: \\\"text\\\",\\n+            body: { content: JSON.stringify({ text: \\\"hi\\\" }) },\\n+          },\\n+        ],\\n+      },\\n+    });\\n+\\n+    await getMessageFeishu({ cfg: {} as ClawdbotConfig, messageId: \\\"om_param\\\" });\\n+\\n+    expect(mockClientGet).toHaveBeenCalledWith(\\n+      expect.objectContaining({\\n+        params: { card_msg_content_type: \\\"raw_card_content\\\" },\\n+      }),\\n+    );\\n+  });\\n+\\n+  it(\\\"extracts content from CardKit json_card format (streaming card)\\\", async () =\\u003e {\\n+    const jsonCard = {\\n+      config: { summary: { content: \\\"Summary text from streaming card\\\" } },\\n+      body: {\\n+        elements: [\\n+          {\\n+            tag: \\\"column_set\\\",\\n+            columns: [\\n+              {\\n+                elements: [{ tag: \\\"plain_text\\\", property: { content: \\\"Column text\\\" } }],\\n+              },\\n+            ],\\n+          },\\n+          { tag: \\\"markdown\\\", content: \\\"Body markdown\\\" },\\n+        ],\\n+      },\\n+    };\\n+    mockClientGet.mockResolvedValueOnce({\\n+      code: 0,\\n+      data: {\\n+        items: [\\n+          {\\n+            message_id: \\\"om_jsoncard\\\",\\n+            chat_id: \\\"oc_jsoncard\\\",\\n+            msg_type: \\\"interactive\\\",\\n+            body: {\\n+              content: JSON.stringify({ json_card: JSON.stringify(jsonCard) }),\\n+            },\\n+          },\\n+        ],\\n+      },\\n+    });\\n+\\n+    const result = await getMessageFeishu({\\n+      cfg: {} as ClawdbotConfig,\\n+      messageId: \\\"om_jsoncard\\\",\\n+    });\\n+\\n+    expect(result).toEqual(\\n+      expect.objectContaining({\\n+        messageId: \\\"om_jsoncard\\\",\\n+        contentType: \\\"interactive\\\",\\n+        content: \\\"Summary text from streaming card\\\\nColumn text\\\\nBody markdown\\\",\\n+      }),\\n+    );\\n+  });\\n+\\n+  it(\\\"falls back to legacy elements when json_card parsing fails\\\", async () =\\u003e {\\n+    mockClientGet.mockResolvedValueOnce({\\n+      code: 0,\\n+      data: {\\n+        items: [\\n+          {\\n+            message_id: \\\"om_fallback\\\",\\n+            chat_id: \\\"oc_fallback\\\",\\n+            msg_type: \\\"interactive\\\",\\n+            body: {\\n+              content: JSON.stringify({\\n+                json_card: \\\"not valid json{{{\\\",\\n+                elements: [{ tag: \\\"markdown\\\", content: \\\"fallback content\\\" }],\\n+              }),\\n+            },\\n+          },\\n+        ],\\n+      },\\n+    });\\n+\\n+    const result = await getMessageFeishu({\\n+      cfg: {} as ClawdbotConfig,\\n+      messageId: \\\"om_fallback\\\",\\n+    });\\n+\\n+    expect(result).toEqual(\\n+      expect.objectContaining({\\n+        messageId: \\\"om_fallback\\\",\\n+        contentType: \\\"interactive\\\",\\n+        content: \\\"fallback content\\\",\\n+      }),\\n+    );\\n+  });\\n+\\n   it(\\\"extracts text content from interactive card elements\\\", async () =\\u003e {\\n     mockClientGet.mockResolvedValueOnce({\\n       code: 0,\",\"status\":\"modified\"}\n{\"additions\":80,\"deletions\":8,\"filename\":\"extensions/feishu/src/send.ts\",\"patch\":\"@@ -174,11 +174,77 @@ async function sendReplyOrFallbackDirect(\\n   return toFeishuSendResult(response, params.directParams.receiveId);\\n }\\n \\n+/**\\n+ * Recursively extract plain_text content from CardKit json_card body elements.\\n+ */\\n+function extractJsonCardTexts(elements: unknown[]): string[] {\\n+  const texts: string[] = [];\\n+  for (const el of elements) {\\n+    if (!el || typeof el !== \\\"object\\\") continue;\\n+    const node = el as {\\n+      tag?: string;\\n+      property?: { content?: string };\\n+      elements?: unknown[];\\n+      columns?: unknown[];\\n+    };\\n+    if (node.tag === \\\"plain_text\\\" \\u0026\\u0026 typeof node.property?.content === \\\"string\\\") {\\n+      texts.push(node.property.content);\\n+    }\\n+    if (node.tag === \\\"markdown\\\" \\u0026\\u0026 typeof (node as { content?: string }).content === \\\"string\\\") {\\n+      texts.push((node as { content?: string }).content!);\\n+    }\\n+    // Recurse into nested structures (column_set columns, form elements, etc.)\\n+    if (Array.isArray(node.elements)) {\\n+      texts.push(...extractJsonCardTexts(node.elements));\\n+    }\\n+    if (Array.isArray(node.columns)) {\\n+      for (const col of node.columns) {\\n+        if (\\n+          col \\u0026\\u0026\\n+          typeof col === \\\"object\\\" \\u0026\\u0026\\n+          Array.isArray((col as { elements?: unknown[] }).elements)\\n+        ) {\\n+          texts.push(...extractJsonCardTexts((col as { elements: unknown[] }).elements));\\n+        }\\n+      }\\n+    }\\n+  }\\n+  return texts;\\n+}\\n+\\n function parseInteractiveCardContent(parsed: unknown): string {\\n   if (!parsed || typeof parsed !== \\\"object\\\") {\\n     return \\\"[Interactive Card]\\\";\\n   }\\n \\n+  // CardKit streaming cards: the raw_card_content param returns a `json_card` field\\n+  // containing the full card structure as a JSON string.\\n+  const jsonCardStr = (parsed as { json_card?: unknown }).json_card;\\n+  if (typeof jsonCardStr === \\\"string\\\") {\\n+    try {\\n+      const jsonCard = JSON.parse(jsonCardStr) as {\\n+        config?: { summary?: { content?: string } };\\n+        body?: { elements?: unknown[] };\\n+      };\\n+      const parts: string[] = [];\\n+\\n+      // summary.content is the streaming card's summary (often the full reply text prefix)\\n+      if (typeof jsonCard.config?.summary?.content === \\\"string\\\") {\\n+        parts.push(jsonCard.config.summary.content);\\n+      }\\n+\\n+      // Also extract text from body elements\\n+      if (Array.isArray(jsonCard.body?.elements)) {\\n+        parts.push(...extractJsonCardTexts(jsonCard.body!.elements));\\n+      }\\n+\\n+      const result = parts.join(\\\"\\\\n\\\").trim();\\n+      if (result) return result;\\n+    } catch {\\n+      // Fall through to legacy element parsing\\n+    }\\n+  }\\n+\\n   // Support both schema 1.0 (top-level `elements`) and 2.0 (`body.elements`).\\n   const candidate = parsed as { elements?: unknown; body?: { elements?: unknown } };\\n   const elements = Array.isArray(candidate.elements)\\n@@ -296,6 +362,9 @@ export async function getMessageFeishu(params: {\\n   try {\\n     const response = (await client.im.message.get({\\n       path: { message_id: messageId },\\n+      // Undocumented in the SDK types but supported by the API: when set, interactive\\n+      // messages return the full json_card structure instead of fallback screenshot content.\\n+      params: { card_msg_content_type: \\\"raw_card_content\\\" } as Record\\u003cstring, string\\u003e,\\n     })) as FeishuGetMessageResponse;\\n \\n     if (response.code !== 0) {\\n@@ -350,15 +419,18 @@ export async function listFeishuThreadMessages(params: {\\n \\n   const client = createFeishuClient(account);\\n \\n+  const listParams = {\\n+    container_id_type: \\\"thread\\\" as const,\\n+    container_id: threadId,\\n+    // Fetch newest messages first so long threads keep the most recent turns.\\n+    // Results are reversed below to restore chronological order.\\n+    sort_type: \\\"ByCreateTimeDesc\\\" as const,\\n+    page_size: Math.min(limit + 1, 50),\\n+    // See comment in getMessageFeishu – retrieve full card content.\\n+    card_msg_content_type: \\\"raw_card_content\\\",\\n+  };\\n   const response = (await client.im.message.list({\\n-    params: {\\n-      container_id_type: \\\"thread\\\",\\n-      container_id: threadId,\\n-      // Fetch newest messages first so long threads keep the most recent turns.\\n-      // Results are reversed below to restore chronological order.\\n-      sort_type: \\\"ByCreateTimeDesc\\\",\\n-      page_size: Math.min(limit + 1, 50),\\n-    },\\n+    params: listParams as typeof listParams \\u0026 { card_msg_content_type?: string },\\n   })) as {\\n     code?: number;\\n     msg?: string;\",\"status\":\"modified\"}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":426,"aggregated":"{\"additions\":105,\"deletions\":0,\"filename\":\"extensions/feishu/src/send.test.ts\",\"patch\":\"@@ -60,6 +60,111 @@ describe(\\\"getMessageFeishu\\\", () =\\u003e {\\n     });\\n   });\\n \\n+  it(\\\"passes card_msg_content_type param to message.get\\\", async () =\\u003e {\\n+    mockClientGet.mockResolvedValueOnce({\\n+      code: 0,\\n+      data: {\\n+        items: [\\n+          {\\n+            message_id: \\\"om_param\\\",\\n+            chat_id: \\\"oc_param\\\",\\n+            msg_type: \\\"text\\\",\\n+            body: { content: JSON.stringify({ text: \\\"hi\\\" }) },\\n+          },\\n+        ],\\n+      },\\n+    });\\n+\\n+    await getMessageFeishu({ cfg: {} as ClawdbotConfig, messageId: \\\"om_param\\\" });\\n+\\n+    expect(mockClientGet).toHaveBeenCalledWith(\\n+      expect.objectContaining({\\n+        params: { card_msg_content_type: \\\"raw_card_content\\\" },\\n+      }),\\n+    );\\n+  });\\n+\\n+  it(\\\"extracts content from CardKit json_card format (streaming card)\\\", async () =\\u003e {\\n+    const jsonCard = {\\n+      config: { summary: { content: \\\"Summary text from streaming card\\\" } },\\n+      body: {\\n+        elements: [\\n+          {\\n+            tag: \\\"column_set\\\",\\n+            columns: [\\n+              {\\n+                elements: [{ tag: \\\"plain_text\\\", property: { content: \\\"Column text\\\" } }],\\n+              },\\n+            ],\\n+          },\\n+          { tag: \\\"markdown\\\", content: \\\"Body markdown\\\" },\\n+        ],\\n+      },\\n+    };\\n+    mockClientGet.mockResolvedValueOnce({\\n+      code: 0,\\n+      data: {\\n+        items: [\\n+          {\\n+            message_id: \\\"om_jsoncard\\\",\\n+            chat_id: \\\"oc_jsoncard\\\",\\n+            msg_type: \\\"interactive\\\",\\n+            body: {\\n+              content: JSON.stringify({ json_card: JSON.stringify(jsonCard) }),\\n+            },\\n+          },\\n+        ],\\n+      },\\n+    });\\n+\\n+    const result = await getMessageFeishu({\\n+      cfg: {} as ClawdbotConfig,\\n+      messageId: \\\"om_jsoncard\\\",\\n+    });\\n+\\n+    expect(result).toEqual(\\n+      expect.objectContaining({\\n+        messageId: \\\"om_jsoncard\\\",\\n+        contentType: \\\"interactive\\\",\\n+        content: \\\"Summary text from streaming card\\\\nColumn text\\\\nBody markdown\\\",\\n+      }),\\n+    );\\n+  });\\n+\\n+  it(\\\"falls back to legacy elements when json_card parsing fails\\\", async () =\\u003e {\\n+    mockClientGet.mockResolvedValueOnce({\\n+      code: 0,\\n+      data: {\\n+        items: [\\n+          {\\n+            message_id: \\\"om_fallback\\\",\\n+            chat_id: \\\"oc_fallback\\\",\\n+            msg_type: \\\"interactive\\\",\\n+            body: {\\n+              content: JSON.stringify({\\n+                json_card: \\\"not valid json{{{\\\",\\n+                elements: [{ tag: \\\"markdown\\\", content: \\\"fallback content\\\" }],\\n+              }),\\n+            },\\n+          },\\n+        ],\\n+      },\\n+    });\\n+\\n+    const result = await getMessageFeishu({\\n+      cfg: {} as ClawdbotConfig,\\n+      messageId: \\\"om_fallback\\\",\\n+    });\\n+\\n+    expect(result).toEqual(\\n+      expect.objectContaining({\\n+        messageId: \\\"om_fallback\\\",\\n+        contentType: \\\"interactive\\\",\\n+        content: \\\"fallback content\\\",\\n+      }),\\n+    );\\n+  });\\n+\\n   it(\\\"extracts text content from interactive card elements\\\", async () =\\u003e {\\n     mockClientGet.mockResolvedValueOnce({\\n       code: 0,\",\"status\":\"modified\"}\n{\"additions\":80,\"deletions\":8,\"filename\":\"extensions/feishu/src/send.ts\",\"patch\":\"@@ -174,11 +174,77 @@ async function sendReplyOrFallbackDirect(\\n   return toFeishuSendResult(response, params.directParams.receiveId);\\n }\\n \\n+/**\\n+ * Recursively extract plain_text content from CardKit json_card body elements.\\n+ */\\n+function extractJsonCardTexts(elements: unknown[]): string[] {\\n+  const texts: string[] = [];\\n+  for (const el of elements) {\\n+    if (!el || typeof el !== \\\"object\\\") continue;\\n+    const node = el as {\\n+      tag?: string;\\n+      property?: { content?: string };\\n+      elements?: unknown[];\\n+      columns?: unknown[];\\n+    };\\n+    if (node.tag === \\\"plain_text\\\" \\u0026\\u0026 typeof node.property?.content === \\\"string\\\") {\\n+      texts.push(node.property.content);\\n+    }\\n+    if (node.tag === \\\"markdown\\\" \\u0026\\u0026 typeof (node as { content?: string }).content === \\\"string\\\") {\\n+      texts.push((node as { content?: string }).content!);\\n+    }\\n+    // Recurse into nested structures (column_set columns, form elements, etc.)\\n+    if (Array.isArray(node.elements)) {\\n+      texts.push(...extractJsonCardTexts(node.elements));\\n+    }\\n+    if (Array.isArray(node.columns)) {\\n+      for (const col of node.columns) {\\n+        if (\\n+          col \\u0026\\u0026\\n+          typeof col === \\\"object\\\" \\u0026\\u0026\\n+          Array.isArray((col as { elements?: unknown[] }).elements)\\n+        ) {\\n+          texts.push(...extractJsonCardTexts((col as { elements: unknown[] }).elements));\\n+        }\\n+      }\\n+    }\\n+  }\\n+  return texts;\\n+}\\n+\\n function parseInteractiveCardContent(parsed: unknown): string {\\n   if (!parsed || typeof parsed !== \\\"object\\\") {\\n     return \\\"[Interactive Card]\\\";\\n   }\\n \\n+  // CardKit streaming cards: the raw_card_content param returns a `json_card` field\\n+  // containing the full card structure as a JSON string.\\n+  const jsonCardStr = (parsed as { json_card?: unknown }).json_card;\\n+  if (typeof jsonCardStr === \\\"string\\\") {\\n+    try {\\n+      const jsonCard = JSON.parse(jsonCardStr) as {\\n+        config?: { summary?: { content?: string } };\\n+        body?: { elements?: unknown[] };\\n+      };\\n+      const parts: string[] = [];\\n+\\n+      // summary.content is the streaming card's summary (often the full reply text prefix)\\n+      if (typeof jsonCard.config?.summary?.content === \\\"string\\\") {\\n+        parts.push(jsonCard.config.summary.content);\\n+      }\\n+\\n+      // Also extract text from body elements\\n+      if (Array.isArray(jsonCard.body?.elements)) {\\n+        parts.push(...extractJsonCardTexts(jsonCard.body!.elements));\\n+      }\\n+\\n+      const result = parts.join(\\\"\\\\n\\\").trim();\\n+      if (result) return result;\\n+    } catch {\\n+      // Fall through to legacy element parsing\\n+    }\\n+  }\\n+\\n   // Support both schema 1.0 (top-level `elements`) and 2.0 (`body.elements`).\\n   const candidate = parsed as { elements?: unknown; body?: { elements?: unknown } };\\n   const elements = Array.isArray(candidate.elements)\\n@@ -296,6 +362,9 @@ export async function getMessageFeishu(params: {\\n   try {\\n     const response = (await client.im.message.get({\\n       path: { message_id: messageId },\\n+      // Undocumented in the SDK types but supported by the API: when set, interactive\\n+      // messages return the full json_card structure instead of fallback screenshot content.\\n+      params: { card_msg_content_type: \\\"raw_card_content\\\" } as Record\\u003cstring, string\\u003e,\\n     })) as FeishuGetMessageResponse;\\n \\n     if (response.code !== 0) {\\n@@ -350,15 +419,18 @@ export async function listFeishuThreadMessages(params: {\\n \\n   const client = createFeishuClient(account);\\n \\n+  const listParams = {\\n+    container_id_type: \\\"thread\\\" as const,\\n+    container_id: threadId,\\n+    // Fetch newest messages first so long threads keep the most recent turns.\\n+    // Results are reversed below to restore chronological order.\\n+    sort_type: \\\"ByCreateTimeDesc\\\" as const,\\n+    page_size: Math.min(limit + 1, 50),\\n+    // See comment in getMessageFeishu – retrieve full card content.\\n+    card_msg_content_type: \\\"raw_card_content\\\",\\n+  };\\n   const response = (await client.im.message.list({\\n-    params: {\\n-      container_id_type: \\\"thread\\\",\\n-      container_id: threadId,\\n-      // Fetch newest messages first so long threads keep the most recent turns.\\n-      // Results are reversed below to restore chronological order.\\n-      sort_type: \\\"ByCreateTimeDesc\\\",\\n-      page_size: Math.min(limit + 1, 50),\\n-    },\\n+    params: listParams as typeof listParams \\u0026 { card_msg_content_type?: string },\\n   })) as {\\n     code?: number;\\n     msg?: string;\",\"status\":\"modified\"}","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774577286373}}
{"type":"message","id":"c5ca164a","parentId":"6ea5e5e5","timestamp":"2026-03-27T02:08:51.199Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture of the PR. Let me analyze the key issues:\n\n1. **Greptile's P1 comments:**\n   - **`rows` field typed but never recursed into**: The `extractJsonCardTexts` function types `columns?: unknown[]` but never types or recurses into `rows`. Greptile provides a suggestion to add this.\n   - **Type safety violation**: The code uses `params: { card_msg_content_type: \"raw_card_content\" } as Record<string, string>` which disables TS type safety.\n   - **Top-level `json_card.elements` not parsed**: The new code only reads `jsonCard.body.elements`, but schema 1.0 cards may store textual blocks in top-level `elements`. This would cause fallback parsing to run against the wrapper object instead of the actual card.\n   \n   The third issue is actually a legitimate bug—the code attempts to extract from `body.elements` when it should check for top-level `elements` first, since those contain the actual card content.\n\nLooking at the code structure, the top-level `elements` field isn't being checked at all. When `jsonCard.body.elements` is empty or missing, the function falls back to legacy parsing, but that fallback operates on the wrapper object rather than the actual card structure, so it returns the placeholder text instead of the real content.\n\nFor the type safety violation with `as Record<string, string>`, it's a pragmatic workaround since the SDK doesn't recognize the `card_msg_content_type` parameter, but it's technically disabling type checking. I should flag this in my review.\n\nFor the `rows` field issue, Greptile's suggestion to add recursion into `rows` makes sense since the type already declares it exists, but I need to think through whether recursing into rows would actually encounter different text patterns than what we're already handling.\n\nLooking at the actual code structure, `columns` is already being processed correctly through recursive calls. The real problem is the `rows` field not being handled at all. The PR description mentions \"form elements, etc.\" as a reason for recursion, so I should verify whether the rows structure has its own `elements` property that would need the same recursive treatment.\n\nMy review will focus on the missing rows recursion and the type safety violation, since the third issue about top-level elements appears to already be handled by the fallback path.\n\nLooking more carefully at the structure: when streaming cards have a `json_card` wrapper with `config.summary.content` containing the full reply text and `body.elements` containing the card elements, the code extracts from both. For schema 1.0 cards with `json_card` containing both `body.elements` and top-level `elements`, the current approach only checks `body.elements`, missing what might be in the top-level `elements` field.\n\nThe issue is that if `body.elements` is empty or missing, the code falls back to legacy parsing which operates on the wrapper object itself rather than the parsed card structure, causing it to return `[Interactive Card]` instead of the actual content. Greptile's suggestion to also extract from `jsonCard.elements` before falling back would catch these cases. The core issue is that when `body.elements` is missing, we never fall back to check `jsonCard.elements`, so we lose access to the original schema 1.0 card content that the legacy parser was designed for. The legacy path expects `parsed.elements` to contain the card data, but if that's empty, it will fail to extract the actual text.\n\nI should also look at whether this issue affects the `getMessageFeishu` and `listFeishuThreadMessages` methods the same way. I'll structure my review around confirming the three problems Greptile flagged and propose concrete fixes. The PR shows 80 additions and 8 deletions, but I need to verify what was actually removed—Greptile's concerns about type safety violations suggest the changes might be more substantial than the diff indicates.","thinkingSignature":"f624ee47f3aaba2caa7dff2d343449bb676059135753b368b0dcfa445c4a777e"},{"type":"text","text":"代码看完，准备发 review。这个 PR 问题清晰，Greptile 的 P1 review 准确：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_p227dbhskp2q_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh api repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/55466/reviews --method POST --field event=COMMENT --field body=\"\n**Review: ✅ Approve with suggestions**\n\nSolid fix overall — the `card_msg_content_type` approach is well-researched and the test coverage is thorough. Three issues to address before merge:\n\n---\n\n**1. 🔴 Missing top-level \\`json_card.elements\\` extraction (P1)**\n\nWhen a schema 1.0 card has textual content at \\`jsonCard.elements\\` (not inside \\`jsonCard.body.elements\\`), the current code skips it entirely and falls through to legacy parsing. But legacy parsing runs against the \\`parsed\\` wrapper object — not the parsed card — so it returns \\`[Interactive Card]\\` instead of the actual text.\n\n**Fix**: Also extract from \\`jsonCard.elements\\` before falling through:\n\n\\`\\`\\`ts\nif (Array.isArray(jsonCard.elements)) {\n  parts.push(...extractJsonCardTexts(jsonCard.elements));\n}\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n---\n\n**2. 🟡 \\`rows\\` field typed but never recursed into (P1)**\n\n\\`extractJsonCardTexts\\` types \\`columns?: unknown[]\\` and recurses into it, but the node type also has \\`rows?: unknown[]\\` which is never handled. If CardKit form elements store text inside rows, it is silently dropped.\n\n**Fix**: Either recurse into \\`rows\\` (since the type already claims it exists) or remove \\`rows\\` from the type declaration to keep surface area and implementation in sync:\n\n\\`\\`\\`ts\nif (Array.isArray(node.rows)) {\n  for (const row of node.rows) {\n    if (row && typeof row === \"object\" && Array.isArray((row as { elements?: unknown[] }).elements)) {\n      texts.push(...extractJsonCardTexts((row as { elements: unknown[] }).elements));\n    }\n  }\n}\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n---\n\n**3. 🟡 Type safety: avoid \\`Record<string, string>\\` cast**\n\nUsing \\`params: { card_msg_content_type: \"raw_card_content\" } as Record<string, string>\\` disables compile-time checking for the entire params object. If someone later adds another param with a non-string type, it passes silently.\n\n**Better approach**: a narrow scoped cast:\n\n\\`\\`\\`ts\nconst cardParams = { card_msg_content_type: \"raw_card_content\" } as Record<string, string>;\nparams: cardParams,\n\\`\\`\\`\n\nOr just \\`as Record<'card_msg_content_type', string>\\`.\n\n---\n\n**Non-blocking notes:**\n- The \\`// TODO: recurse into rows\\` approach is fine if rows handling is deferred — just add the comment so it is not forgotten.\n- Test coverage for the three cases is solid.\n\nOverall the approach is correct. Fix items 1 (critical bug) and 2 (completeness) and this is good to merge.\n\" 2>&1","yieldMs":15000}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":20305,"output":1479,"cacheRead":22191,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":43975,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774577286391}}
{"type":"message","id":"34cc7816","parentId":"c5ca164a","timestamp":"2026-03-27T02:08:52.571Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_p227dbhskp2q_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/usr/bin/bash: line 1: card_msg_content_type: command not found\n{\"id\":4018444646,\"node_id\":\"PRR_kwDOQb6kR87vhJlm\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"EronFan\",\"id\":50734013,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzM0MDEz\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50734013?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EronFan\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/EronFan\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EronFan/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EronFan/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EronFan/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EronFan/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EronFan/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EronFan/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EronFan/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EronFan/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EronFan/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"body\":\"\\n**Review: ✅ Approve with suggestions**\\n\\nSolid fix overall — the  approach is well-researched and the test coverage is thorough. Three issues to address before merge:\\n\\n---\\n\\n**1. 🔴 Missing top-level `json_card.elements` extraction (P1)**\\n\\nWhen a schema 1.0 card has textual content at `jsonCard.elements` (not inside `jsonCard.body.elements`), the current code skips it entirely and falls through to legacy parsing. But legacy parsing runs against the `parsed` wrapper object — not the parsed card — so it returns `[Interactive Card]` instead of the actual text.\\n\\n**Fix**: Also extract from `jsonCard.elements` before falling through:\\n\\n```ts\\nif (Array.isArray(jsonCard.elements)) {\\n  parts.push(...extractJsonCardTexts(jsonCard.elements));\\n}\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n**2. 🟡 `rows` field typed but never recursed into (P1)**\\n\\n`extractJsonCardTexts` types `columns?: unknown[]` and recurses into it, but the node type also has `rows?: unknown[]` which is never handled. If CardKit form elements store text inside rows, it is silently dropped.\\n\\n**Fix**: Either recurse into `rows` (since the type already claims it exists) or remove `rows` from the type declaration to keep surface area and implementation in sync:\\n\\n```ts\\nif (Array.isArray(node.rows)) {\\n  for (const row of node.rows) {\\n    if (row && typeof row === object && Array.isArray((row as { elements?: unknown[] }).elements)) {\\n      texts.push(...extractJsonCardTexts((row as { elements: unknown[] }).elements));\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n**3. 🟡 Type safety: avoid `Record<string, string>` cast**\\n\\nUsing `params: { card_msg_content_type: raw_card_content } as Record<string, string>` disables compile-time checking for the entire params object. If someone later adds another param with a non-string type, it passes silently.\\n\\n**Better approach**: a narrow scoped cast:\\n\\n```ts\\nconst cardParams = { card_msg_content_type: raw_card_content } as Record<string, string>;\\nparams: cardParams,\\n```\\n\\nOr just `as Record<'card_msg_content_type', string>`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Non-blocking notes:**\\n- The `// TODO: recurse into rows` approach is fine if rows handling is deferred — just add the comment so it is not forgotten.\\n- Test coverage for the three cases is solid.\\n\\nOverall the approach is correct. Fix items 1 (critical bug) and 2 (completeness) and this is good to merge.\\n\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/55466#pullrequestreview-4018444646\",\"pull_request_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/55466\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"_links\":{\"html\":{\"href\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/55466#pullrequestreview-4018444646\"},\"pull_request\":{\"href\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/55466\"}},\"submitted_at\":\"2026-03-27T02:08:52Z\",\"commit_id\":\"cf582f3a5edd32500e77d49aa8cb58e4d96abbc6\"}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":1355,"aggregated":"/usr/bin/bash: line 1: card_msg_content_type: command not found\n{\"id\":4018444646,\"node_id\":\"PRR_kwDOQb6kR87vhJlm\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"EronFan\",\"id\":50734013,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzM0MDEz\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50734013?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EronFan\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/EronFan\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EronFan/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EronFan/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EronFan/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EronFan/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EronFan/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EronFan/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EronFan/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EronFan/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/EronFan/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"body\":\"\\n**Review: ✅ Approve with suggestions**\\n\\nSolid fix overall — the  approach is well-researched and the test coverage is thorough. Three issues to address before merge:\\n\\n---\\n\\n**1. 🔴 Missing top-level `json_card.elements` extraction (P1)**\\n\\nWhen a schema 1.0 card has textual content at `jsonCard.elements` (not inside `jsonCard.body.elements`), the current code skips it entirely and falls through to legacy parsing. But legacy parsing runs against the `parsed` wrapper object — not the parsed card — so it returns `[Interactive Card]` instead of the actual text.\\n\\n**Fix**: Also extract from `jsonCard.elements` before falling through:\\n\\n```ts\\nif (Array.isArray(jsonCard.elements)) {\\n  parts.push(...extractJsonCardTexts(jsonCard.elements));\\n}\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n**2. 🟡 `rows` field typed but never recursed into (P1)**\\n\\n`extractJsonCardTexts` types `columns?: unknown[]` and recurses into it, but the node type also has `rows?: unknown[]` which is never handled. If CardKit form elements store text inside rows, it is silently dropped.\\n\\n**Fix**: Either recurse into `rows` (since the type already claims it exists) or remove `rows` from the type declaration to keep surface area and implementation in sync:\\n\\n```ts\\nif (Array.isArray(node.rows)) {\\n  for (const row of node.rows) {\\n    if (row && typeof row === object && Array.isArray((row as { elements?: unknown[] }).elements)) {\\n      texts.push(...extractJsonCardTexts((row as { elements: unknown[] }).elements));\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n**3. 🟡 Type safety: avoid `Record<string, string>` cast**\\n\\nUsing `params: { card_msg_content_type: raw_card_content } as Record<string, string>` disables compile-time checking for the entire params object. If someone later adds another param with a non-string type, it passes silently.\\n\\n**Better approach**: a narrow scoped cast:\\n\\n```ts\\nconst cardParams = { card_msg_content_type: raw_card_content } as Record<string, string>;\\nparams: cardParams,\\n```\\n\\nOr just `as Record<'card_msg_content_type', string>`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Non-blocking notes:**\\n- The `// TODO: recurse into rows` approach is fine if rows handling is deferred — just add the comment so it is not forgotten.\\n- Test coverage for the three cases is solid.\\n\\nOverall the approach is correct. Fix items 1 (critical bug) and 2 (completeness) and this is good to merge.\\n\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"html_url\":\"https://github