{"type":"message","id":"c13a3446","parentId":"34cc7816","timestamp":"2026-03-27T02:09:04.745Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The review was submitted, but the body lost the code formatting because the shell interpreted backticks. Let me also reply to Greptile's comments to acknowledge and build on them. But first, let me note the review was submitted.\n\nNow let me update the project file and give the status to the user.","thinkingSignature":"b2e6a26c8c68aa14f7198349d876e193cfc5b796c821ee27c37862d5eaee0e3e"},{"type":"text","text":"Review 已发出，但 shell 把代码格式吃了。让我重新补一条更清晰的评论：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_nj17wghbz7vn_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh api repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/55466/comments --method POST --field body=\"Addressing the 3 Greptile items with the author:\n\n**Item 1 (top-level json_card.elements)**: Confirmed critical. The current code only checks \\`jsonCard.body.elements\\`, missing schema 1.0 cards that store text in \\`jsonCard.elements\\`. Please also extract from \\`jsonCard.elements\\` before falling through to legacy parsing.\n\n**Item 2 (rows recursion)**: Confirmed completeness issue. The \\`rows?: unknown[]\\` field is typed but not handled. Either add rows recursion or remove \\`rows\\` from the type to keep surface area in sync.\n\n**Item 3 (type safety)**: Type cast noted. A narrowly scoped cast (\\`as Record<'card_msg_content_type', string>\\`) would be cleaner than \\`Record<string, string>\\`.\n\nThe PR approach is fundamentally sound and the test coverage is solid. These are all pre-merge fixable items.\" 2>&1","yieldMs":8000}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":22861,"output":332,"cacheRead":22191,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":45384,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774577332570}}
