{"type":"message","id":"8a2728cd","parentId":"bceaf423","timestamp":"2026-03-27T03:38:22.169Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_42myvsx66p2i_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"guoqunabc 2026-03-27T02:20: Thanks for the thorough review @EronFan! All 3 items addressed:\n\n**Item 1 (schem...\nguoqunabc 2026-03-27T02:11: ## CI Failure Analysis\n\nAll CI failures in this PR are **pre-existing on `main`*...\nEronFan 2026-03-27T02:09: Addressing the 3 Greptile items:\n\n**Item 1 (top-level json_card.elements)**: Con...\ngreptile-apps[bot] 2026-03-27T01:53: <h3>Greptile Summary</h3>\n\nThis PR fixes the inability to read full text content..."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":433,"aggregated":"guoqunabc 2026-03-27T02:20: Thanks for the thorough review @EronFan! All 3 items addressed:\n\n**Item 1 (schem...\nguoqunabc 2026-03-27T02:11: ## CI Failure Analysis\n\nAll CI failures in this PR are **pre-existing on `main`*...\nEronFan 2026-03-27T02:09: Addressing the 3 Greptile items:\n\n**Item 1 (top-level json_card.elements)**: Con...\ngreptile-apps[bot] 2026-03-27T01:53: <h3>Greptile Summary</h3>\n\nThis PR fixes the inability to read full text content...","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774582702154}}
{"type":"message","id":"36533fc8","parentId":"8a2728cd","timestamp":"2026-03-27T03:38:27.444Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There are new comments from the author `guoqunabc` on #55466. They addressed all 3 items in my review! And there's a CI failure analysis showing the failures are pre-existing on main.\n\nLet me fetch more details to see the full response.","thinkingSignature":"d63178a3680fc8870daaa9353c4e14e3caab33687308cab44a79c5800e70081b"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_becq5l89a0zb_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh api repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/55466/comments --jq 'sort_by(.created_at) | reverse | .[0:4] | .[] | {user: .user.login, body: .body}' 2>&1 | head -100","yieldMs":8000}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":25070,"output":145,"cacheRead":22191,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":47406,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774582702168}}
{"type":"message","id":"fe66f17e","parentId":"36533fc8","timestamp":"2026-03-27T03:38:27.890Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_becq5l89a0zb_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"body\":\"Thanks for the thorough review @EronFan! All 3 items addressed:\\n\\n**Item 1 (schema 1.0 elements)**: Fixed — now also extracts from `jsonCard.elements` (top-level) in addition to `jsonCard.body.elements`. Schema 1.0 cards are covered.\\n\\n**Item 2 (rows recursion)**: Already removed in the previous commit — confirmed `rows` is no longer in the type declaration.\\n\\n**Item 3 (type cast)**: For `getMessageFeishu`, the SDK's `message.get` params type requires an index-signature-compatible type, so `Record\\u003cstring, string\\u003e` is the narrowest cast that compiles (a single-key Record triggers TS2559). For `listFeishuThreadMessages`, the cast already uses `typeof listParams \\u0026 { card_msg_content_type?: string }` which is more precise.\\n\\nChanges pushed — CI should re-run shortly.\",\"user\":\"guoqunabc\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CI Failure Analysis\\n\\nAll CI failures in this PR are **pre-existing on `main`** and unrelated to our changes.\\n\\n### Evidence\\n\\nOur PR only modifies `extensions/feishu/src/send.ts` and `extensions/feishu/src/send.test.ts`. The feishu-specific CI job (`extension-fast-feishu`) **passes**.\\n\\n**Main branch CI (run [23627455328](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/23627455328)) also fails** the same jobs:\\n- `check-additional` — config-docs-drift + plugin-sdk-api-drift (baseline regeneration needed after upstream refactors)\\n- `checks-fast-contracts-protocol` — `runtime.contract.test.ts` openai-codex OAuth refresh test\\n- `checks-fast-extensions` — matrix Jiti proxy `ownKeys` TypeError (irc/config-schema.ts)\\n- `checks-node-test-1/2/3/4` — timeouts in registry/catalog/bundled-web-search contracts, cron owner-auth, config validation allowed-values\\n- `checks-windows-node-test-2/3/6` — same timeout failures on Windows\\n\\n**`build-smoke`** (memory: 409.4 MB RSS vs 400 MB limit) is marginal and not caused by our +66 lines of pure function code. Main passes this at the boundary — it is a known flaky check.\\n\\n### Our Changes\\n\\n- ✅ `extension-fast-feishu` — **PASS**\\n- ✅ No `server-chat.ts` or `server-chat.agent-events.test.ts` modifications (clean diff)\\n- ✅ Only `send.ts` (add `extractJsonCardTexts` + `json_card` parsing) and `send.test.ts` (corresponding tests)\",\"user\":\"guoqunabc\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressing the 3 Greptile items:\\n\\n**Item 1 (top-level json_card.elements)**: Confirmed critical. The code only checks jsonCard.body.elements, missing schema 1.0 cards that store text in jsonCard.elements. Please also extract from jsonCard.elements before falling through to legacy parsing.\\n\\n**Item 2 (rows recursion)**: Confirmed completeness issue. The rows field is typed but not handled in extractJsonCardTexts. Either add rows recursion or remove rows from the type.\\n\\n**Item 3 (type safety)**: Type cast noted. A narrowly scoped cast (as Record\\u003c'card_msg_content_type', string\\u003e) would be cleaner than Record\\u003cstring, string\\u003e.\\n\\nOverall the approach is sound and the test coverage is solid. These are all pre-merge fixable items.\",\"user\":\"EronFan\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003ch3\\u003eGreptile Summary\\u003c/h3\\u003e\\n\\nThis PR fixes the inability to read full text content from Feishu CardKit streaming cards by passing the undocumented `card_msg_content_type=raw_card_content` query parameter to both the single-message and thread-list IM API calls. It also adds a `json_card` parsing branch (with recursive element extraction) that runs before the existing legacy `elements`/`body.elements` path, and extends the `buildSessionEventSnapshot` helper in `server-chat.ts` to promote several additional session metadata fields to the top level of the broadcast payload.\\n\\n- `send.ts`: `card_msg_content_type` added to both `message.get` and `message.list`; new `extractJsonCardTexts` helper recursively extracts `plain_text` and `markdown` content from column/element trees; `parseInteractiveCardContent` tries the `json_card` path first and gracefully falls through on parse failure.\\n- `send.test.ts`: Three targeted new test cases cover param forwarding, `json_card` parsing (including `column_set` nesting), and JSON parse-error fallback — good coverage of the new code paths.\\n- `server-chat.ts`: Many additional session row fields (`fastMode`, `verboseLevel`, `sendPolicy`, `responseUsage`, etc.) are now promoted to the top level of the session snapshot, bringing it in line with what `session` already exposes nested.\\n- `server-chat.agent-events.test.ts`: New lifecycle test validates that the promoted fields arrive correctly in the broadcast payload.\\n\\n\\u003ch3\\u003eConfidence Score: 4/5\\u003c/h3\\u003e\\n\\nSafe to merge; changes are additive with clean fallback behaviour and solid test coverage.\\n\\nThe core Feishu fix is well-implemented — it adds the undocumented param, parses the new response format, falls back gracefully on parse failure, and is backed by three new tests. The server-chat.ts snapshot expansion is additive and validated by a new test. The one minor inconsistency (the rows field is declared in the type but never iterated over) is a P2 cleanup item that does not affect the primary user path or introduce any regressions.\\n\\nNo files require special attention; extensions/feishu/src/send.ts has one minor type/logic gap around rows worth a follow-up.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003e\\u003ch3\\u003eImportant Files Changed\\u003c/h3\\u003e\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n| Filename | Overview |\\n|----------|----------|\\n| extensions/feishu/src/send.ts | Adds card_msg_content_type=raw_card_content param to both message.get and message.list, and a new extractJsonCardTexts helper + json_card parsing branch in parseInteractiveCardContent. Logic is sound with proper fallback; minor inconsistency between the typed rows field and missing recursion over it. |\\n| extensions/feishu/src/send.test.ts | Three new test cases cover param forwarding, json_card parsing with nested column_set elements, and fallback on invalid JSON — good coverage of the new code paths. |\\n| src/gateway/server-chat.ts | Promotes many additional session row fields (fastMode, verboseLevel, sendPolicy, responseUsage, etc.) to the top level of the session snapshot object. Additive change that mirrors what was already done for totalTokens/contextTokens. |\\n| src/gateway/server-chat.agent-events.test.ts | Adds a lifecycle test validating that promoted session metadata fields are present at the top level of the broadcast payload; also fixes the module mock for loadGatewaySessionRow to prevent test bleed. |\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\u003c!-- greptile_other_comments_section --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt To Fix All With AI\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n`````markdown\\nThis is a comment left during a code review.\\nPath: extensions/feishu/src/send.ts\\nLine: 189-212\\n\\nComment:\\n**`rows` field typed but never recursed into**\\n\\nThe node type includes `rows?: unknown[]`, and the comment references \\\"form elements, etc.\\\" as a motivation for recursion — but there is no corresponding loop over `rows`. Any CardKit elements that store text inside rows (e.g., a `form` element with row-based layout) would be silently skipped.\\n\\nEither add the recursion or remove the `rows` field from the type to keep the declared surface and the implementation in sync:\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    const node = el as {\\n      tag?: string;\\n      property?: { content?: string };\\n      elements?: unknown[];\\n      columns?: unknown[];\\n    };\\n    if (node.tag === \\\"plain_text\\\" \\u0026\\u0026 typeof node.property?.content === \\\"string\\\") {\\n      texts.push(node.property.content);\\n    }\\n    if (node.tag === \\\"markdown\\\" \\u0026\\u0026 typeof (node as { content?: string }).content === \\\"string\\\") {\\n      texts.push((node as { content?: string }).content!);\\n    }\\n    // Recurse into nested structures (column_set columns, form elements, etc.)\\n    if (Array.isArray(node.elements)) {\\n      texts.push(...extractJsonCardTexts(node.elements));\\n    }\\n    if (Array.isArray(node.columns)) {\\n      for (const col of node.columns) {\\n        if (\\n          col \\u0026\\u0026\\n          typeof col === \\\"object\\\" \\u0026\\u0026\\n          Array.isArray((col as { elements?: unknown[] }).elements)\\n        ) {\\n          texts.push(...extractJsonCardTexts((col as { elements: unknown[] }).elements));\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n```\\n\\nOr, if rows are intentionally planned for the future, add a `// TODO: recurse into rows` comment so it is not forgotten.\\n\\nHow can I resolve this? If you propose a fix, please make it concise.\\n`````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003csub\\u003eReviews (1): Last reviewed commit: [\\\"fix(feishu): read full CardKit streaming...\\\"](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/commit/9649267f22b9ae8ded832adedb78581e23303ec6) | [Re-trigger Greptile](https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=26524164)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\",\"user\":\"greptile-apps[bot]\"}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":426,"aggregated":"{\"body\":\"Thanks for the thorough review @EronFan! All 3 items addressed:\\n\\n**Item 1 (schema 1.0 elements)**: Fixed — now also extracts from `jsonCard.elements` (top-level) in addition to `jsonCard.body.elements`. Schema 1.0 cards are covered.\\n\\n**Item 2 (rows recursion)**: Already removed in the previous commit — confirmed `rows` is no longer in the type declaration.\\n\\n**Item 3 (type cast)**: For `getMessageFeishu`, the SDK's `message.get` params type requires an index-signature-compatible type, so `Record\\u003cstring, string\\u003e` is the narrowest cast that compiles (a single-key Record triggers TS2559). For `listFeishuThreadMessages`, the cast already uses `typeof listParams \\u0026 { card_msg_content_type?: string }` which is more precise.\\n\\nChanges pushed — CI should re-run shortly.\",\"user\":\"guoqunabc\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CI Failure Analysis\\n\\nAll CI failures in this PR are **pre-existing on `main`** and unrelated to our changes.\\n\\n### Evidence\\n\\nOur PR only modifies `extensions/feishu/src/send.ts` and `extensions/feishu/src/send.test.ts`. The feishu-specific CI job (`extension-fast-feishu`) **passes**.\\n\\n**Main branch CI (run [23627455328](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/23627455328)) also fails** the same jobs:\\n- `check-additional` — config-docs-drift + plugin-sdk-api-drift (baseline regeneration needed after upstream refactors)\\n- `checks-fast-contracts-protocol` — `runtime.contract.test.ts` openai-codex OAuth refresh test\\n- `checks-fast-extensions` — matrix Jiti proxy `ownKeys` TypeError (irc/config-schema.ts)\\n- `checks-node-test-1/2/3/4` — timeouts in registry/catalog/bundled-web-search contracts, cron owner-auth, config validation allowed-values\\n- `checks-windows-node-test-2/3/6` — same timeout failures on Windows\\n\\n**`build-smoke`** (memory: 409.4 MB RSS vs 400 MB limit) is marginal and not caused by our +66 lines of pure function code. Main passes this at the boundary — it is a known flaky check.\\n\\n### Our Changes\\n\\n- ✅ `extension-fast-feishu` — **PASS**\\n- ✅ No `server-chat.ts` or `server-chat.agent-events.test.ts` modifications (clean diff)\\n- ✅ Only `send.ts` (add `extractJsonCardTexts` + `json_card` parsing) and `send.test.ts` (corresponding tests)\",\"user\":\"guoqunabc\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressing the 3 Greptile items:\\n\\n**Item 1 (top-level json_card.elements)**: Confirmed critical. The code only checks jsonCard.body.elements, missing schema 1.0 cards that store text in jsonCard.elements. Please also extract from jsonCard.elements before falling through to legacy parsing.\\n\\n**Item 2 (rows recursion)**: Confirmed completeness issue. The rows field is typed but not handled in extractJsonCardTexts. Either add rows recursion or remove rows from the type.\\n\\n**Item 3 (type safety)**: Type cast noted. A narrowly scoped cast (as Record\\u003c'card_msg_content_type', string\\u003e) would be cleaner than Record\\u003cstring, string\\u003e.\\n\\nOverall the approach is sound and the test coverage is solid. These are all pre-merge fixable items.\",\"user\":\"EronFan\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003ch3\\u003eGreptile Summary\\u003c/h3\\u003e\\n\\nThis PR fixes the inability to read full text content from Feishu CardKit streaming cards by passing the undocumented `card_msg_content_type=raw_card_content` query parameter to both the single-message and thread-list IM API calls. It also adds a `json_card` parsing branch (with recursive element extraction) that runs before the existing legacy `elements`/`body.elements` path, and extends the `buildSessionEventSnapshot` helper in `server-chat.ts` to promote several additional session metadata fields to the top level of the broadcast payload.\\n\\n- `send.ts`: `card_msg_content_type` added to both `message.get` and `message.list`; new `extractJsonCardTexts` helper recursively extracts `plain_text` and `markdown` content from column/element trees; `parseInteractiveCardContent` tries the `json_card` path first and gracefully falls through on parse failure.\\n- `send.test.ts`: Three targeted new test cases cover param forwarding, `json_card` parsing (including `column_set` nesting), and JSON parse-error fallback — good coverage of the new code paths.\\n- `server-chat.ts`: Many additional session row fields (`fastMode`, `verboseLevel`, `sendPolicy`, `responseUsage`, etc.) are now promoted to the top level of the session snapshot, bringing it in line with what `session` already exposes nested.\\n- `server-chat.agent-events.test.ts`: New lifecycle test validates that the promoted fields arrive correctly in the broadcast payload.\\n\\n\\u003ch3\\u003eConfidence Score: 4/5\\u003c/h3\\u003e\\n\\nSafe to merge; changes are additive with clean fallback behaviour and solid test coverage.\\n\\nThe core Feishu fix is well-implemented — it adds the undocumented param, parses the new response format, falls back gracefully on parse failure, and is backed by three new tests. The server-chat.ts snapshot expansion is additive and validated by a new test. The one minor inconsistency (the rows field is declared in the type but never iterated over) is a P2 cleanup item that does not affect the primary user path or introduce any regressions.\\n\\nNo files require special attention; extensions/feishu/src/send.ts has one minor type/logic gap around rows worth a follow-up.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003e\\u003ch3\\u003eImportant Files Changed\\u003c/h3\\u003e\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n| Filename | Overview |\\n|----------|----------|\\n| extensions/feishu/src/send.ts | Adds card_msg_content_type=raw_card_content param to both message.get and message.list, and a new extractJsonCardTexts helper + json_card parsing branch in parseInteractiveCardContent. Logic is sound with proper fallback; minor inconsistency between the typed rows field and missing recursion over it. |\\n| extensions/feishu/src/send.test.ts | Three new test cases cover param forwarding, json_card parsing with nested column_set elements, and fallback on invalid JSON — good coverage of the new code paths. |\\n| src/gateway/server-chat.ts | Promotes many additional session row fields (fastMode, verboseLevel, sendPolicy, responseUsage, etc.) to the top level of the session snapshot object. Additive change that mirrors what was already done for totalTokens/contextTokens. |\\n| src/gateway/server-chat.agent-events.test.ts | Adds a lifecycle test validating that promoted session metadata fields are present at the top level of the broadcast payload; also fixes the module mock for loadGatewaySessionRow to prevent test bleed. |\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\u003c!-- greptile_other_comments_section --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt To Fix All With AI\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n`````markdown\\nThis is a comment left during a code review.\\nPath: extensions/feishu/src/send.ts\\nLine: 189-212\\n\\nComment:\\n**`rows` field typed but never recursed into**\\n\\nThe node type includes `rows?: unknown[]`, and the comment references \\\"form elements, etc.\\\" as a motivation for recursion — but there is no corresponding loop over `rows`. Any CardKit elements that store text inside rows (e.g., a `form` element with row-based layout) would be silently skipped.\\n\\nEither add the recursion or remove the `rows` field from the type to keep the declared surface and the implementation in sync:\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    const node = el as {\\n      tag?: string;\\n      property?: { content?: string };\\n      elements?: unknown[];\\n      columns?: unknown[];\\n    };\\n    if (node.tag === \\\"plain_text\\\" \\u0026\\u0026 typeof node.property?.content === \\\"string\\\") {\\n      texts.push(node.property.content);\\n    }\\n    if (node.tag === \\\"markdown\\\" \\u0026\\u0026 typeof (node as { content?: string }).content === \\\"string\\\") {\\n      texts.push((node as { content?: string }).content!);\\n    }\\n    // Recurse into nested structures (column_set columns, form elements, etc.)\\n    if (Array.isArray(node.elements)) {\\n      texts.push(...extractJsonCardTexts(node.elements));\\n    }\\n    if (Array.isArray(node.columns)) {\\n      for (const col of node.columns) {\\n        if (\\n          col \\u0026\\u0026\\n          typeof col === \\\"object\\\" \\u0026\\u0026\\n          Array.isArray((col as { elements?: unknown[] }).elements)\\n        ) {\\n          texts.push(...extractJsonCardTexts((col as { elements: unknown[] }).elements));\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n```\\n\\nOr, if rows are intentionally planned for the future, add a `// TODO: recurse into rows` comment so it is not forgotten.\\n\\nHow can I resolve this? If you propose a fix, please make it concise.\\n`````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003csub\\u003eReviews (1): Last reviewed commit: [\\\"fix(feishu): read full CardKit streaming...\\\"](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/commit/9649267f22b9ae8ded832adedb78581e23303ec6) | [Re-trigger Greptile](https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=26524164)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\",\"user\":\"greptile-apps[bot]\"}","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774582707870}}
{"type":"message","id":"38c57cbe","parentId":"fe66f17e","timestamp":"2026-03-27T03:38:43.690Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The author `guoqunabc` has addressed all 3 items in my review:\n\n1. Item 1 (schema 1.0 elements): Fixed — now extracts from `jsonCard.elements` (top-level) in addition to `jsonCard.body.elements`\n2. Item 2 (rows recursion): Already removed in previous commit — `rows` is no longer in the type declaration\n3. Item 3 (type cast): Explained that for `getMessageFeishu`, the SDK's `message.get` params type requires an index-signature-compatible type, so `Record<string, string>` is the narrowest cast that compiles\n\nThe CI failures are pre-existing on `main` and unrelated to the PR changes.\n\n\nI should acknowledge the author's response and note that the PR looks ready to merge pending CI completion, while also considering whether there are other PRs worth reviewing given today's activity level.","thinkingSignature":"6557b31640271e2702563ffd55b164e9a0f3494ee0eef159855881e6f050fc62"},{"type":"text","text":"重大进展！**#55466 作者 `guoqunabc` 回复了**，全部 3 项都已修复：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_pes48a0eaafd_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh api repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/55466/reviews --jq '.[] | \"\\(.author.login) \\(.state) \\(.body[0:100])...\"' 2>&1","yieldMs":8000}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":27473,"output":285,"cacheRead":22191,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":49949,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774582707889}}
