{"type":"message","id":"0a8fd5d2","parentId":"d609e829","timestamp":"2026-03-27T11:06:48.227Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have details on both. Let me check the existing comments on #55479 to understand what's already been said, so I don't duplicate.\n\nFor #55479, there's 1 comment. Let me see it.\n\nFor #55458, there's 1 comment too. Let me see it.","thinkingSignature":"51a7ef6dfaf95b23173cbb66cde3b4f1929de357b855a0e312cd331d59cccb1b"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_23twqvd0hinj_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh api repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/55479/comments --jq '.[].body' 2>/dev/null","timeout":10}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":18590,"output":119,"cacheRead":22191,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":40900,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774609603315}}
{"type":"message","id":"17bc89f5","parentId":"0a8fd5d2","timestamp":"2026-03-27T11:06:48.659Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_23twqvd0hinj_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I also reproduced this with fresh session IDs across multiple specialist agents (`investor`, `creator`, `engineer`), and the bundled-only `systemPromptReport.skills.entries` result was consistent across them."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":413,"aggregated":"I also reproduced this with fresh session IDs across multiple specialist agents (`investor`, `creator`, `engineer`), and the bundled-only `systemPromptReport.skills.entries` result was consistent across them.","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774609608640}}
{"type":"message","id":"0bc4969b","parentId":"17bc89f5","timestamp":"2026-03-27T11:06:51.491Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, the existing comment on #55479 is from the author confirming the repro. Let me also check #55458 comments.","thinkingSignature":"ad6e2e337419371e3b0710feceb422420dd4a82c4a1a572856a8bf2a965613ae"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_4huly6z6psd9_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh api repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/55458/comments --jq '.[].body' 2>/dev/null","timeout":10}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":18764,"output":86,"cacheRead":22191,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":41041,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774609608655}}
{"type":"message","id":"38600d2c","parentId":"0bc4969b","timestamp":"2026-03-27T11:06:51.988Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_4huly6z6psd9_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=7\" align=\"top\"></a> **Falsy guard silently drops empty-string errors**\n\nThe conditional spread `...(probeError ? { probeError } : {})` will omit `probeError` from the return value when an `Error` is thrown with an empty message (i.e. `new Error(\"\")`). This is the one case where the probe truly failed but the new surface still silently hides it — the opposite of the PR's intent. `memory.probeError` would be `undefined` and the `if (memory.probeError)` guard in `status.command.ts` would also pass right over it.\n\nSince `probeError?: string` is already declared as optional on `MemoryStatusSnapshot`, spreading it directly is cleaner and avoids the edge case:\n\n```suggestion\n  return { agentId, ...status, probeError };\n```\n\nIf an explicit presence check is preferred, guard on `!== undefined` instead.\n\n<details><summary>Prompt To Fix With AI</summary>\n\n`````markdown\nThis is a comment left during a code review.\nPath: src/commands/status.scan.ts\nLine: 183\n\nComment:\n**Falsy guard silently drops empty-string errors**\n\nThe conditional spread `...(probeError ? { probeError } : {})` will omit `probeError` from the return value when an `Error` is thrown with an empty message (i.e. `new Error(\"\")`). This is the one case where the probe truly failed but the new surface still silently hides it — the opposite of the PR's intent. `memory.probeError` would be `undefined` and the `if (memory.probeError)` guard in `status.command.ts` would also pass right over it.\n\nSince `probeError?: string` is already declared as optional on `MemoryStatusSnapshot`, spreading it directly is cleaner and avoids the edge case:\n\n```suggestion\n  return { agentId, ...status, probeError };\n```\n\nIf an explicit presence check is preferred, guard on `!== undefined` instead.\n\nHow can I resolve this? If you propose a fix, please make it concise.\n`````\n</details>\n**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve explicit OpenAI provider selection**\n\nThis deduplication treats `openai` as unavailable whenever `openai-codex` is already recorded for `OPENAI_API_KEY`, even though both providers are valid with that same key. In the model selection block below, `!availableProviders.includes(currentProvider)` then becomes true for an explicitly configured `openai/...` primary, so startup rewrites it to Codex on every run and can also drop OpenAI fallbacks. This breaks the script’s stated goal of preserving user overrides in `openclaw.json`.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Use valid awk quoting for Docker key fingerprint parsing**\n\nThe awk program is single-quoted, so the embedded `\\\"` is passed literally and causes an awk parse error (`backslash not last character on line`). When `OPENCLAW_INSTALL_DOCKER_CLI` is enabled, this assignment exits non-zero and aborts the Docker build before fingerprint verification completes.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":478,"aggregated":"<a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=7\" align=\"top\"></a> **Falsy guard silently drops empty-string errors**\n\nThe conditional spread `...(probeError ? { probeError } : {})` will omit `probeError` from the return value when an `Error` is thrown with an empty message (i.e. `new Error(\"\")`). This is the one case where the probe truly failed but the new surface still silently hides it — the opposite of the PR's intent. `memory.probeError` would be `undefined` and the `if (memory.probeError)` guard in `status.command.ts` would also pass right over it.\n\nSince `probeError?: string` is already declared as optional on `MemoryStatusSnapshot`, spreading it directly is cleaner and avoids the edge case:\n\n```suggestion\n  return { agentId, ...status, probeError };\n```\n\nIf an explicit presence check is preferred, guard on `!== undefined` instead.\n\n<details><summary>Prompt To Fix With AI</summary>\n\n`````markdown\nThis is a comment left during a code review.\nPath: src/commands/status.scan.ts\nLine: 183\n\nComment:\n**Falsy guard silently drops empty-string errors**\n\nThe conditional spread `...(probeError ? { probeError } : {})` will omit `probeError` from the return value when an `Error` is thrown with an empty message (i.e. `new Error(\"\")`). This is the one case where the probe truly failed but the new surface still silently hides it — the opposite of the PR's intent. `memory.probeError` would be `undefined` and the `if (memory.probeError)` guard in `status.command.ts` would also pass right over it.\n\nSince `probeError?: string` is already declared as optional on `MemoryStatusSnapshot`, spreading it directly is cleaner and avoids the edge case:\n\n```suggestion\n  return { agentId, ...status, probeError };\n```\n\nIf an explicit presence check is preferred, guard on `!== undefined` instead.\n\nHow can I resolve this? If you propose a fix, please make it concise.\n`````\n</details>\n**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve explicit OpenAI provider selection**\n\nThis deduplication treats `openai` as unavailable whenever `openai-codex` is already recorded for `OPENAI_API_KEY`, even though both providers are valid with that same key. In the model selection block below, `!availableProviders.includes(currentProvider)` then becomes true for an explicitly configured `openai/...` primary, so startup rewrites it to Codex on every run and can also drop OpenAI fallbacks. This breaks the script’s stated goal of preserving user overrides in `openclaw.json`.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Use valid awk quoting for Docker key fingerprint parsing**\n\nThe awk program is single-quoted, so the embedded `\\\"` is passed literally and causes an awk parse error (`backslash not last character on line`). When `OPENCLAW_INSTALL_DOCKER_CLI` is enabled, this assignment exits non-zero and aborts the Docker build before fingerprint verification completes.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774609611970}}
